WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.338 --> 00:00:02.739
- You can smell death.

00:00:02.739 --> 00:00:04.094
I could walk into a place and I know

00:00:04.094 --> 00:00:06.261
there's a corpse in there.

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:10.422
(spooky music)

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.941
- Hi, my name is Angela Gilmore-Manning.

00:00:15.941 --> 00:00:19.763
- I'm Jean Daleus from Roy
L. Gilmore's funeral home,

00:00:19.763 --> 00:00:23.930
and hope today I've answered
a few questions that you had.

00:00:27.802 --> 00:00:30.717
- With unclaimed bodies, normally the city

00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:34.786
will take possession, repossess the body.

00:00:34.786 --> 00:00:37.248
In other words, if they're homeless,

00:00:37.248 --> 00:00:40.079
they'll go to the extent where they will

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:43.891
try to get in touch with
a family member or so.

00:00:43.891 --> 00:00:46.618
If not, you go to Potter's Field.

00:00:46.618 --> 00:00:50.785
Potter's Field is a general
cemetery for homeless folks.

00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:55.650
That's what they call city burial.

00:00:57.806 --> 00:01:00.940
To prepare a body is to preserve the body.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.101
That's through the process of embalming.

00:01:03.101 --> 00:01:04.912
The embalming process is just

00:01:04.912 --> 00:01:07.448
like you're performing surgery.

00:01:07.448 --> 00:01:09.537
Based on the way you approach it,

00:01:09.537 --> 00:01:11.607
you have to know what
the person died from,

00:01:11.607 --> 00:01:14.199
so you know how to preserve the body.

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:18.029
- So, what we're doing is
we're using the carotid artery

00:01:18.029 --> 00:01:22.443
to inject fluid to preserve
the tissue; the body tissue.

00:01:22.443 --> 00:01:24.422
As we're doing that simultaneously,

00:01:24.422 --> 00:01:27.755
we're draining through the carotid vein.

00:01:30.188 --> 00:01:34.138
- The only time you
smell something would be

00:01:34.138 --> 00:01:36.778
once the body's been there for a few days

00:01:36.778 --> 00:01:40.452
and once you die, you undergo
certain chemical changes

00:01:40.452 --> 00:01:43.477
on the inside which will reflect

00:01:43.477 --> 00:01:44.923
on your physical appearance.

00:01:44.923 --> 00:01:47.089
That's when you start deteriorating.

00:01:47.089 --> 00:01:49.006
There you have an odor.

00:01:51.692 --> 00:01:55.020
The way we deal with smell is
when you're in the prep room,

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.176
you have to be equipped.

00:01:57.176 --> 00:01:59.564
Put on your mask, and the mask,

00:01:59.564 --> 00:02:03.430
they have filters where
you don't get the odor

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:05.819
that's emanating from the body.

00:02:05.819 --> 00:02:10.107
To add to that, once the body is embalmed,

00:02:10.107 --> 00:02:11.524
there is no odor.

00:02:15.471 --> 00:02:18.034
As you know an autopsy
is a process where they

00:02:18.034 --> 00:02:20.631
sample every organ in the body.

00:02:20.631 --> 00:02:23.637
Then, when the body arrives
at the funeral home,

00:02:23.637 --> 00:02:25.670
we have to put the person back together.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:29.087
The organs are placed back into the body.

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.359
- We're not actually doing the

00:02:33.359 --> 00:02:35.472
cremation here on the premises.

00:02:35.472 --> 00:02:39.639
We have to go to a crematory
in order to cremate the body.

00:02:42.813 --> 00:02:46.123
Not all funeral services
have open caskets.

00:02:46.123 --> 00:02:50.873
It's really designed to have
a viewing for the family.

00:02:50.873 --> 00:02:52.824
They do that because it's traditional

00:02:52.824 --> 00:02:55.337
for some families, not all families.

00:02:55.337 --> 00:02:59.004
Some families choose
to have closed caskets.

00:03:00.787 --> 00:03:05.182
- Techniques and then they
have equipment such as a lift.

00:03:05.182 --> 00:03:07.174
You could use a lift with straps.

00:03:07.174 --> 00:03:09.985
I would caution anyone, again,

00:03:09.985 --> 00:03:13.318
you don't try to lift dead weight, okay?

00:03:14.342 --> 00:03:17.497
You use certain techniques
to move bodies around.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:20.014
That's why they have lifts.

00:03:20.014 --> 00:03:24.000
You could use the lifts to
navigate inside the prep room

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.833
and to place bodies where
you want them to be.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.918
- Our death certificates are obtained

00:03:31.918 --> 00:03:34.463
through the doctor when someone passes

00:03:34.463 --> 00:03:38.314
either at home or
hospital or nursing home.

00:03:38.314 --> 00:03:41.517
The original death certificate
is signed by a doctor.

00:03:41.517 --> 00:03:43.495
Once we receive that signature,

00:03:43.495 --> 00:03:46.328
then we're able to claim the body.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.345
My father told me years
ago that funeral homes were

00:03:50.345 --> 00:03:53.746
designed like homes because
they were homes for the dead.

00:03:53.746 --> 00:03:57.417
Years ago, when families
had loved ones to pass on,

00:03:57.417 --> 00:04:01.334
they used to be posed in
their homes initially.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:09.607
- Actually they don't, only on
the exterior of the building.

00:04:11.293 --> 00:04:12.583
Not on the inside.

00:04:12.583 --> 00:04:14.650
On the inside, it's just
like everyone go to bed

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.381
and go to sleep so the lights are off.

00:04:17.381 --> 00:04:19.859
But, on the exterior of the building,

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:23.776
to see the entity yes
the lights have to be on.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.487
Love of working and also knowing that

00:04:31.487 --> 00:04:34.146
I'm out here helping a family.

00:04:34.146 --> 00:04:37.293
- How I keep my spirits
lifted knowing that

00:04:37.293 --> 00:04:41.185
I'm here to assist families in making

00:04:41.185 --> 00:04:43.084
funeral arrangements for their loved one

00:04:43.084 --> 00:04:45.001
with dignity and honor.

00:04:46.001 --> 00:04:48.918
(mysterious music)

